### DASHBOARD API - Combined Scenarios
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Scenario 1: Dashboard Initial Load
# Call these in sequence to populate a dashboard

# Step 1: Get summary KPIs
GET {{baseUrl}}/getDashboardSummary()
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Step 2: Get recent cases for table
GET {{baseUrl}}/listCases(limit=10)
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Step 3: Get supplier risk overview
GET {{baseUrl}}/getSupplierRiskOverview()
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Step 4: Get inventory alerts
GET {{baseUrl}}/getInventoryHealth()
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Scenario 2: Case Detail View
# When user clicks on a case

# Get full case details
GET {{baseUrl}}/getCaseDetail(caseId='CASE-1001')
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Get case timeline/history
GET {{baseUrl}}/getCaseHistory(caseId='CASE-1001')
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Scenario 3: Risk Dashboard
# For risk-focused dashboard view

# Get risk analytics
GET {{baseUrl}}/getRiskAnalytics()
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Get high-risk cases
GET {{baseUrl}}/listCases(priority='Critical')
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Get supplier risk data
GET {{baseUrl}}/getSupplierRiskOverview()
Content-Type: application/json

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### DASHBOARD API - OData Entity Queries
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Get Case Histories Entity
GET {{baseUrl}}/CaseHistories
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Get Case Histories for Specific Case
GET {{baseUrl}}/CaseHistories?$filter=caseId eq 'CASE-1001'
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Get Early Warning Results with High Risk
GET {{baseUrl}}/EarlyWarningResults?$filter=riskLevel eq 'HIGH'
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Get Survival Results Requiring Action
GET {{baseUrl}}/SurvivalResults?$filter=actionRequired eq true
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Get Cases by Event Type
GET {{baseUrl}}/Cases?$filter=eventType eq 'PO_DELAY'&$orderby=createdAt desc
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Get Cases with Recommendation
GET {{baseUrl}}/Cases?$filter=recommendation ne null&$select=caseId,status,priority,recommendation
Content-Type: application/json

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SUPPLIER HISTORICAL OTIF
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ------------------------------------------
### Get Historical OTIF for a Supplier (with defaults: last 6 months, max 50 POs)
### Replace 'SUPPLIER_ID' with actual supplier ID from your S/4HANA system
### ------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/supplier-resilience/getSupplierHistoricalOtif(supplierId='0000001234')
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ------------------------------------------
### Get Historical OTIF with Custom Date Range
### ------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/supplier-resilience/getSupplierHistoricalOtif(supplierId='0000001234',fromDate='2026-01-01',toDate='2026-08-13')
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ------------------------------------------
### Get Historical OTIF - Example with 10-digit supplier ID
### SAP suppliers are typically 10 digits with leading zeros
### ------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/supplier-resilience/getSupplierHistoricalOtif(supplierId='0000017300')
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ------------------------------------------
### Get Historical OTIF - Last 3 months only
### ------------------------------------------
# Calculate 3 months ago from today for fromDate
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/supplier-resilience/getSupplierHistoricalOtif(supplierId='0000001234',fromDate='2026-05-13',toDate='2026-08-13')
Content-Type: application/json

###

